{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-15T03:53:05.372Z","author":"claude-hub","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0400d60929071b1beaa422c1","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.300","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-github-2o9k"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"closeout cannot close items in trackers that require structured close fields"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found while dogfooding pm github closeout on 2026-10-15. pm-rust's tracker enforces strict close validation, so pm close requires resolution, expected_result and actual_result. closeout passes only a close reason, so pm github closeout --apply on pm-rust PR 81 failed on the first item ('missing resolution, expected_result, actual_result'), wrote nothing (it failed closed) and left all seven delivered items open; the orchestrator closed them by hand. closeout should populate the structured fields from the same verifiable GitHub facts it already uses (resolution: delivered by the PR, with merge and head SHAs; expected_result: the item's acceptance criteria when present; actual_result: merged, with the passing required checks), never from PR body or comment text, and should report clearly when a tracker policy still refuses the close."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["closeout","validation"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-15T03:53:05.372Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-15T03:53:05.372Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"claude-hub"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"On a tracker with strict close validation, closeout --apply closes every eligible item with resolution, expected_result and actual_result derived only from GitHub facts and the item's own acceptance criteria; the fields contain no PR body or comment text; a tracker that refuses the close for another reason yields a skip row with that reason instead of aborting the remaining plan; tests cover strict and default validation trackers"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-github-t4i2","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:53:05.372Z","author":"claude-hub","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"9a4d9d3de361594e88e70099f432a2c00bf6d2ef63429b18897834f2e77aa1df","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"1ddbd9ea2421b43a81976ceb9c68f476f4037042f11c83fa935cb8f67e515455"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-15T04:40:14.473Z","author":"claude-hub","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0400d60929071b1beaa422c1","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.300","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"On a tracker with strict close validation, closeout --apply closes every eligible item with resolution, expected_result and actual_result derived only from GitHub facts and the item's own acceptance criteria. When an item has no acceptance criteria, expected_result falls back to a fixed sentence built only from GitHub facts (for example: delivered by the linked pull request, merged with its required checks passing). Generated fields never restate a defect-shaped item title as the delivered behaviour, and contain no PR body or comment text. A tracker that refuses the close for another reason yields a skip row with that reason instead of aborting the remaining plan. Tests cover strict and default validation trackers, and items with and without acceptance criteria."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-15T04:40:14.473Z"}],"before_hash":"9a4d9d3de361594e88e70099f432a2c00bf6d2ef63429b18897834f2e77aa1df","after_hash":"55d72e42d30e6292c2889b0b6dbec9f5d9ee86d4574964a3cbac51e7003ae5d5","item_hash_version":3,"message":"Define the missing-criteria fallback and the defect-shaped title rule","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"c6383cac74f88b077d9b881b95f06cd320b8874689d77cb304ae2019cc075e65"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-15T04:40:15.269Z","author":"claude-hub","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0400d60929071b1beaa422c1","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.300","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-15T04:40:15.269Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-15T04:40:15.269Z","author":"claude-hub","text":"Spec refinements from review: (a) CodeRabbit on PR 125: eligible in_progress items may lack acceptance criteria, so expected_result needs a fallback built only from GitHub facts, and tests must cover that case. (b) CodeRabbit on pm-rust PR 82: hand-written close fields that restated the defect-shaped title of pm-rust-poen ('Legacy list cursors without after_index publish the query fingerprint') read as if the fix shipped the defect, and had to be corrected by an appended update. Generated fields must not restate a defect-shaped title as the delivered behaviour."}]}],"before_hash":"55d72e42d30e6292c2889b0b6dbec9f5d9ee86d4574964a3cbac51e7003ae5d5","after_hash":"f31376e5959345f89b624e15a278ce6c650b576f421bc8aec9288253198d11ba","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"963c51173162cea5181a0cd309d9ae62db367e12c92b73fee9fda108dec25c50"}
