{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-15T06:49:23.673Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"56b095c4742cd4c1c73ebc48","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-15T06:49:23.673Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Packed real-data proof: a scratch clone of unbraind/pm-rust at f182da3~1 (a5656636d280aa30d11810b28350a6ff2ca3bd5e) kept strict close validation. Installed only the packed package there; PR 81 dry-run planned seven closes and two eligibility skips, apply closed all seven with zero failures. Read back pm-rust-poen and pm-rust-cqk7: expected_result equals acceptance_criteria verbatim; resolution contains PR URL and 12-character merge/head SHAs; actual_result contains only merge time and verified check names. Repeat apply closed zero with item/history hashes unchanged. No scratch push. Evidence: docs/strict-closeout-proof.md. The complete linked test suite exceeded its default 120-second timeout; increased its declared timeout to 600 seconds for the rerun without changing test or coverage scope."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-15T06:49:23.673Z"}],"before_hash":"bc29b6ca0f8a17460f38dc22c1afd232580ef392c9a2054a433bfbf0057da4e4","after_hash":"bd6b8328165198130226a49a209a7a817dff8a012d9db3b8963b514ff2f7b679","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"d099ea04c904c17