{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-15T09:25:49.431Z","author":"claude-hub","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0400d60929071b1beaa422c1","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.300","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/7","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-15T09:25:49.431Z","author":"claude-hub","text":"Review round 1 (PR 126, CodeRabbit on bbf6516), fixed by the orchestrator: under the fallback rule (no readable required contexts) the generated actual_result and the fallback expected_result claimed 'required checks passing', even when only neutral or skipped runs existed. checkEvidence now describes the applied policy: 'required checks passing: <names>' for the required rule, and for the fallback rule 'no readable required checks, so every completed head check run had to succeed, be neutral or be skipped; successful checks: <names>' or '…; no check reported success'. The fallback expected_result reads 'merged after its head check gate passed'. New test 'fallback closes describe the applied check policy and never claim required checks'. Gates: isolated npm and bun release:check 662/662 at 100% coverage. The same PR closes pm-github-wrmt (delivered by PR 122) through closeout; it was the in_progress item that failed today's scheduled release (tracked as pm-github-l1ot)."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-15T09:25:49.431Z"}],"before_hash":"82edb051f7bee1b4a10f3ba02400908adbf898d20a242fb42d32811feaae77dc","after_hash":"3dbdc9a84923eabe3aec1bf48e56e15f580e4b62a01d8a4e515a92b55be6f0c2","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","res